{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents, once every group is decided, to commit the agreed requirements of all groups in one commit before any implementation, leaving out uncommitted edits the user said do not belong to the task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.commit` says the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to do three things:\n1. Commit only once every group is decided.\n2. Commit all groups' agreed requirements in one commit, before any implementation.\n3. Leave out uncommitted edits the user said do not belong to the task.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_commits_every_group_together_before_code]` carries `{test}` for the requirement. It runs against the bundled `habeas-requirements` skill text. The `step_of` and `step` helpers parse the numbered workflow steps, so each assertion is tied to a specific step.\n\n**Mapping.**\n- *One commit, all groups, before code.* `step_of(SKILL, \"then commit it, all groups together, before any code\")` panics unless some workflow step contains that phrase. It finds step 5 in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, whose text reads \"…then commit it, all groups together, before any code; leave out unrelated edits found in step 1\".\n- *Leaving out edits that do not belong.* `step(SKILL, commit).contains(\"leave out unrelated edits found in step 1\")` checks that the commit step itself carries the exclusion. Step 1 of the skill runs `git status` and asks the user whether uncommitted edits belong to the task. The test therefore ties the exclusion to the user's answer. Step 1's ask-the-user behaviour is covered by the separate test `the_requirements_skill_asks_about_foreign_edits_before_drafting`, so it needs no check here.\n- *Only once every group is decided.* `assert!(commit > step_of(SKILL, \"**Gate:**\"))` requires the commit step to come after the gate step. Step 4 holds the gate: \"no implementation or test code, and no commit, until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group\". The gate text itself is covered by the separate `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.agreement` test, so it needs no check here.\n\n**Counterexamples the test would catch.**\n- The commit step is dropped or reworded to commit per group.\n- The \"before any code\" wording is removed.\n- The leave-out sentence is removed or moved out of the commit step.\n- The commit step is moved before the gate.\n\nThe requirement names no other modes or boundaries. I found no untested obligation and no assertion that contradicts the text. There are no acknowledgments.",
